-
-- Backend-driven, periodic: default every **6 h** (`FLEET_SYNC_INTERVAL_S`,
-  min 5 min sanity floor inherited from the poll pattern), anonymous FTP in a
-  worker thread; immediate first sync on service start; manual
-  `POST /api/fleet-status/sync`.
-- Per cycle: one FTP session; `dac/incois` NLIST (membership); per float
-  Rtraj MDTM+SIZE and `profiles/` listing fingerprint (sorted
-  name:size:mtime sha1); download + parse only on change; parsed rows cached,
-  bytes discarded.
-- Cache: `decoder-ui/data/fleet_status/cache.json` (atomic tmp+rename, same
-  pattern as `ingestion.json`); survives restarts and FTP outages.
-- Failure semantics: transport/float errors never break the page — last valid
-  rows are retained, `sync.status` becomes `degraded`/`error`, the UI shows
-  last successful sync time + error + stale banner. Per-float errors are kept
-  beside the retained row.
